    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d203">

                <pb facs="0190" n="180" xml:id="pg180"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.6363/463: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-10-02T14:00:00-03:00">October 2, 1941—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>418. With reference to section 2 of the Department’s telegram no. 250, September
                        29.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d203-f1"/> As reported in my despatch 184 of
                    September 26, the oil pool plan is being studied by an advisory board designated
                    for the purpose by the Uruguayan Government. I shall do everything practicable
                    to expedite a favorable decision.</p>
                <p>From confidential statements made to me by a high Ancap official I infer that the
                    Uruguayans have sought information regarding the attitude of the Argentine,
                    Brazilian and possibly other facilities. The official remarked confidentially
                    that he understood the Brazilian attitude to be unfavorable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
